---
interface Props {
  section: 'idea' | 'philosophy' | 'status' | 'final';
}

const { section } = Astro.props;
---

{section === 'idea' && (
  <section class="section idea-section" id="idea" aria-labelledby="idea-heading">
    <div class="shell editorial-layout">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">BACK TO BASICS</p>
        <h2 class="section-heading" id="idea-heading">You shouldn't need a complicated IDE to run ten lines of Java.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <p class="body-copy">Modern development tools are extraordinarily capable. But not every task needs an enormous workspace, dozens of panels, or a complex project configuration.</p>
        <ul class="idea-uses" role="list">
          <li>Sometimes you want to try an algorithm.</li>
          <li>Understand how an API behaves.</li>
          <li>Write a small program.</li>
          <li>Fix a bug.</li>
          <li>Or simply learn Java.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="body-copy">That's what TurboJ is for.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">A focused editor built around the shortest possible path between an idea and a running program.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{section === 'philosophy' && (
  <section class="section philosophy-section" id="philosophy" aria-labelledby="philosophy-heading">
    <div class="shell editorial-layout">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">WHY TURBOJ EXISTS</p>
        <h2 class="section-heading" id="philosophy-heading">Good tools get out of your way.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <p class="body-copy">TurboJ isn't trying to replace every feature of a full-scale IDE.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">It doesn't need to.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">It's built for those moments when all you want is an editor, a compiler, and a running Java program.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">The tools we remember weren't always the ones with the longest feature lists.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">They were the ones that made it easy to get things done.</p>
        <p class="section-closing">Old-school focus. Modern Java.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{section === 'status' && (
  <section class="section status-section" id="status" aria-labelledby="status-heading">
    <div class="shell editorial-layout">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">UNDER ACTIVE DEVELOPMENT</p>
        <h2 class="section-heading" id="status-heading">The editor is running. We're just getting started.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <p class="body-copy">TurboJ has moved beyond a concept.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">The first working editor can open Java source, compile, run programs, and display execution output in its classic interface.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">The next focus is improving the editing and execution loop, measuring latency, and making the application reliable enough for others to use.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">We'll share builds, documentation, and source-code links when they're ready for public use.</p>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="#demo">Back to the editor</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{section === 'final' && (
  <section class="section final-section" aria-labelledby="final-heading">
    <div class="shell final-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow">READY_</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading" id="final-heading">Remember the joy of just writing code?</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">We're bringing it back.</p>
      <p class="final-brand">TurboJ — The ultra-fast Java editor.</p>
      <p class="final-tagline">Old-school focus. Modern Java.</p>
      <a class="button" href="#demo">Explore the editor</a>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
